  "_comment": "open-fdd point names (the Haystack names a package map uses, and the SQL roles the historian stores) -> CAMBER roles. Written from open-fdd's public documentation at the pinned commit; no open-fdd code or SQL is copied. A row with camber_role null is a deliberate non-mapping: CAMBER has no role with that meaning, or mapping it would change what a rule measures; the reason says which. quantity names the unit conversion applied for --units si (see docs/INTEROP-OPENFDD.md). equip_types, when present, limits a row to those open-fdd equipment stamps.",
  "equip_types": {
    "ahu": "AHU",
    "rtu": "RTU",
    "vav": "VAV",
    "chwPlant": "CHW_PLANT",
    "boiler": "BOILER",
    "heatPump": "HEAT_PUMP",
    "weather": "WEATHER",
    "meter": "METER",
    "fanCoil": "FCU",
    "fcu": "FCU",
    "zone_other": "ZONE_OTHER"
  },
